<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Committee of Public Safety</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1793–1795</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Committee of Public Safety was the executive body set up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-convention">French National Convention</a> in April 1793 to direct the war and suppress internal revolt. Dominated from July 1793 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilien-robespierre">Maximilien Robespierre</a> and his allies, it ran the Reign of Terror, in which thousands of suspected enemies of the Revolution were executed. Its power collapsed after Robespierre's fall in July 1794, and it was abolished in 1795.</p></div>
